From 0353066c38af3ca849e99f012af38920643d950d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:11:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(auth): R6.3 - capture worker identities; re-enumerate
 before use; unverifiable enumeration blocks

Incremental after baseline + R4 + R5 + R6 + R6.1 + R6.2. Draft; not deployed.
- staleWorkerGuard: each evaluation records the actual active-worker object of every
  registration when it is enumerated and compares those recorded identities after a second
  enumeration (registration.active is a live property); an in-place change discards the
  evaluation. stillCurrent() re-reads each captured registration; new confirm() enumerates
  again and requires every active worker to be one that was probed as current.
- enumeration that rejects, throws, hangs, is not a list or has malformed entries is
  UNVERIFIED: blocked (previously read as 'no workers')
- recoveryRun: awaits confirm() then stillCurrent() immediately before the session is
  used, cancellable across the awaits
- tests: reproduction of the R6.2 failure, identity/enumeration/confirm suites, integrated
  guard+run scenarios, mutation checks; Chromium D8 scenarios and R6.2 negative control

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NvuEKCqEak8vUZ3RsxZA4i
